00:02:03.023 --> 00:02:05.590
<i>When I was a
kid, in the summer,</i>


00:02:05.623 --> 00:02:07.590
<i>I would go up
into northern Canada</i>


00:02:07.623 --> 00:02:10.424
<i>with my father
and two brothers fishing.</i>


00:02:10.457 --> 00:02:12.956
<i>The one male bonding
thing we did.</i>


00:02:12.989 --> 00:02:16.490
<i>And the only extravagance my
rather workaholic, miserly good,</i>


00:02:16.523 --> 00:02:19.657
<i>country-boy father
could muster.</i>


00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:24.023
<i>We flew by bush plane,
small planes with pontoons,</i>


00:02:24.056 --> 00:02:27.424
<i>into a wilderness lake where we
would be met by an old trapper</i>


00:02:27.457 --> 00:02:29.623
<i>who lived there year-round.</i>


00:02:29.657 --> 00:02:32.956
<i>He hadn't been back
to civilization for 20 years,</i>


00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:38.889
<i>and communicated with the fish camp
organizers on a shortwave radio.</i>


00:02:38.923 --> 00:02:42.490
<i>Once we got to his camp,
a group of small cabins</i>


00:02:42.523 --> 00:02:44.523
<i>nestled around
his little house,</i>


00:02:44.557 --> 00:02:46.590
<i>with the sides
stacked head high</i>


00:02:46.623 --> 00:02:49.358
<i>with a mountain of dried bones.</i>


00:02:49.391 --> 00:02:53.956
<i>Behind, there were teepees with
a small group of Cree Indians</i>


00:02:53.989 --> 00:02:57.657
<i>who would take us out
on the water and be our guides.</i>


00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:04.224
<i>They had names like Tom Pitt,
Rod Rat, Billy Deer.</i>


00:03:04.257 --> 00:03:07.889
<i>All toothless, passive,
and alcoholic.</i>


00:03:07.923 --> 00:03:11.291
<i>However, they were not allowed
liquor while they worked.</i>


00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:14.923
<i>Although their eyes always were
an angry, bloodshot red,</i>


00:03:14.956 --> 00:03:17.590
<i>so maybe they were
sneaking drinks.</i>


00:03:17.623 --> 00:03:21.157
<i>They truly were
romantic figures gone to seed.</i>


00:03:21.191 --> 00:03:23.590
<i>Anyway, the point.</i>


00:03:23.623 --> 00:03:26.457
<i>At this camp,
there was a group of huskies</i>


00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:29.889
<i>that that trapper kept for his
dogsled for work in the winter.</i>


00:03:29.923 --> 00:03:31.623
<i>It wasn't until
we stopped going</i>


00:03:31.657 --> 00:03:35.056
<i>that this guy got rid of them
for a snowmobile.</i>


00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:39.590
<i>These dogs were sweet,
but wild enough to be scary.</i>


00:03:39.623 --> 00:03:43.923
<i>The biggest manhood challenge
for me at six years old</i>


00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.324
<i>was running from our cabin
to the outhouse,</i>


00:03:46.357 --> 00:03:50.090
<i>because the dogs would chase
you and nip at your heels.</i>


00:03:50.124 --> 00:03:52.157
<i>While you were in the outhouse,</i>


00:03:52.191 --> 00:03:54.623
<i>they would scratch at the door
and growl.</i>


00:03:54.657 --> 00:03:56.324
<i>Horrific.</i>


00:03:56.357 --> 00:03:59.291
<i>And then,
when you were through,</i>


00:03:59.324 --> 00:04:01.657
<i>you'd race back
to the safety of your cabin</i>


00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:04.956
<i>hoping the nips
wouldn't turn into bites.</i>


00:06:07.091 --> 00:06:08.323
Okay.


00:06:09.323 --> 00:06:10.623
Rum it is.


00:06:46.457 --> 00:06:49.290
